{"id":14743,"artist":"Jekyll And Hyde Musical","title":"The World Has Gone Insane","lyrics_plain":"Tim Shrimpton\nJEKYLL:\nThe world has gone insane!\nAnd parasites are eating at my brain!\nAnd nothing is the way it was before!\nA pack of wolves is howling at my door!\nI'm living in a nonstop nightmare!\nDead men's dreams!\nFilled with screaming pain!\nHurling me to mad extremes\nin a world that's gone insane!\nThe world has lost its head\nAnd every evil hour is filled with dread!\nI'm floating on a lake, but upside down!\nAnd when I try to breathe I start to drown!\nI cannot speak\nas nameless ghosts and faceless ghouls\nbid me join the dead!\nNo one tells these gruesome fools\nThat the world has lost its head!\nFiendish creatures leave their graves to taunt me!\nOld friends risen from the dead to haunt me!\nGod-forsaken images that daunt me\nDrowning in an endless flood of blood!\nThe world has lost its mind!\nAnd everywhere I turn, I fear I'll find\nSome nightmare even worse then those I see!\nSantanic demons closing in on me!\nHow can it be\nThat even though they see my plight,\nEveryone is blind!\nNight is day and day is night!\nIn a world that's lost its mind!\nThe world has gone berserk!\nAnd hiding in the murk, new monsters lurk!\nI see a sea of snakes upon the floor!\nI see the reaper grinning at my door!\nI scream in silence:\nBad is good and good is bad!\nSacred is profane!\nAnd it's wiser to be mad...\nHYDE:\nIn a world that's gone insane!","lyrics_synced":"[00:00.00] Tim Shrimpton\n[00:19.77] JEKYLL:\n[00:20.55] The world has gone insane!\n[00:22.77] And parasites are eating at my brain!\n[00:25.68] And nothing is the way it was before!\n[00:28.59] A pack of wolves is howling at my door!\n[00:31.50] I'm living in a nonstop nightmare!\n[00:33.86] Dead men's dreams!\n[00:35.32] Filled with screaming pain!\n[00:38.23] Hurling me to mad extremes\n[00:40.77] in a world that's gone insane!\n[00:49.62] The world has lost its head\n[00:51.86] And every evil hour is filled with dread!\n[00:54.77] I'm floating on a lake, but upside down!\n[00:57.68] And when I try to breathe I start to drown!\n[01:00.59] I cannot speak\n[01:01.32] as nameless ghosts and faceless ghouls\n[01:04.41] bid me join the dead!\n[01:07.32] No one tells these gruesome fools\n[01:09.86] That the world has lost its head!\n[01:16.04] Fiendish creatures leave their graves to taunt me!\n[01:21.86] Old friends risen from the dead to haunt me!\n[01:27.68] God-forsaken images that daunt me\n[01:32.77] Drowning in an endless flood of blood!\n[01:39.14] The world has lost its mind!\n[01:41.32] And everywhere I turn, I fear I'll find\n[01:44.23] Some nightmare even worse then those I see!\n[01:47.14] Santanic demons closing in on me!\n[01:50.04] How can it be\n[01:50.77] That even though they see my plight,\n[01:53.86] Everyone is blind!\n[01:56.77] Night is day and day is night!\n[01:59.32] In a world that's lost its mind!\n[02:05.32] The world has gone berserk!\n[02:07.50] And hiding in the murk, new monsters lurk!\n[02:10.41] I see a sea of snakes upon the floor!\n[02:13.32] I see the reaper grinning at my door!\n[02:16.23] I scream in silence:\n[02:17.14] Bad is good and good is bad!\n[02:20.04] Sacred is profane!\n[02:22.95] And it's wiser to be mad...\n[02:27.32] HYDE:\n[02:28.41] In a world that's gone insane!","lyrics_synced_enhanced":"[00:19.77] <00:19.77>JEKYLL:\n[00:20.54] <00:20.54>The <00:20.77>world <00:21.31>has <00:21.49>gone <00:22.04>in <00:22.22>sane!\n[00:22.77] <00:22.77>And <00:22.95>par <00:23.13>a <00:23.31>sites <00:23.49>are <00:23.68>eat <00:24.22>ing <00:24.40>at <00:24.95>my <00:25.13>brain!\n[00:25.68] <00:25.68>And <00:25.86>noth <00:26.04>ing <00:26.22>is <00:26.40>the <00:26.59>way <00:27.13>it <00:27.31>was <00:27.86>be <00:28.04>fore!\n[00:28.59] <00:28.59>A <00:28.77>pack <00:28.95>of <00:29.13>wolves <00:29.31>is <00:29.49>howl <00:30.04>ing <00:30.22>at <00:30.77>my <00:30.95>door!\n[00:31.49] <00:31.49>I'm <00:31.68>liv <0